## Modern-UX principles (baked into every screen)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Mobile-first (~80% of salon bookings are mobile) · guest checkout, no forced account ·
visible progress indicator · full price + deposit transparency up front · primary CTA
above the fold · real-time availability with reasons + next-opening suggestion · minimal
fields + inline validation + forgiving recovery · layered reminders (confirm + 24h + 2h)
with one-tap reschedule · consented, unavoidable cancellation policy · photo-forward,
on-brand, app-like feel · rich client profiles that personalize + carry prep notes into
confirmations.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Build order (single pass, sequenced sanely)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
0. **Local Supabase stack** (CLI) + one canonical migration (fixed schema, RLS,
   concurrency constraints, slot-hold TTL, new tables) + one canonical seed
   (real QueenG catalog, cents). Generate `database.types.ts`.
1. Supabase client trio (browser/server/admin) + Auth (magic link) + `lib/pricing.ts`
   + shared money/date utils (timezone-safe).
2. Booking engine: duration-aware availability API → slot-hold create → intake + photo
   upload → Stripe deposit checkout → appointment **pending** → confirmation email/SMS.
   Concurrency-safe via transactional RPC.
3. Confirm/decline flow (secure admin API, decline auto-refunds w/ policy-aware amount) +
   admin dashboard shell + pending queue + calendar.
4. Client account (auth, history, self-service reschedule/cancel within policy).
5. Storefront wired to DB (services, portfolio, reviews) + fix NAP + real map + contact form.
6. Reminders cron (idempotent) + slot-hold cleanup cron.
7. Growth features: waitlist, rebooking, review automation, CRM, finance CSV, analytics.
8. SEO, accessibility, performance, polish; verify `next build` + local end-to-end run;
   deploy notes for Vercel + hosted Supabase.

